Tokenization:

Step 1: Create a struct
include variable types
Terminals:

-Operators = &&, ||
-Commands = characters
-Group = ( )
-Punctuations = -, ', ", 
-Redidrectors = < << > >>
-Stringliterals/words = characters


command_line → pipeline ( "||" pipeline | "&&" pipeline )*
pipeline     → command ( "|" command )*
command      → assignment | simple_command | subshell
assignment   → NAME "=" STRING
simple_command → WORD (WORD)*
subshell     → "(" command_line ")"
redirection  → ("<" | ">" | "<<" | ">>") WORD

command_line  → pipeline (("&&" | "||") pipeline)*
pipeline      → command ("|" command)*
command       → (assignment | simple_command | subshell) redirection*
assignment    → NAME "=" STRING
simple_command → WORD (WORD)*
subshell      → "(" command_line ")"
redirection   → ("<" | ">" | "<<" | ">>") WORD

🧱 4. So the rule is
Context	Can redirection appear here?	Example
Before command	✅	>out cat file
After command name	✅	cat >out file
Between arguments	✅	cat file1 >out file2
After all arguments	✅	cat file >out
Between assignment and command	❌	VAR=value >out echo hi
Between assignment words	❌	VAR=value >out OTHER=1 echo hi
Inside a word	❌	e>filecho


typedef struct s_expression
{
    char *operators
    char *commands
    char *group
    char *punctuation
    char *redirection
    char *string
       
}   t_expression